## What happens

It checks nothing, and fails anyway.

The sweep was interrupted, when 15 of its 28 planned runs had ended, so the counts below are of the runs that ended. Its confirm runs didn't all end: 3 of its 16 did, and they are of those.

At [6351c869](https://github.com/example/repo/commit/6351c86978a51659d1d1dae16a9f4553bd64a712), with go1.27.0 on 8 cores, `flaky stress` ran it 3 times:

|       | load 1 | load 2 |
|-------|--------|--------|
| cpu 1 | 1 / 2  | 0 / 1  |
| cpu 2 | 0 / 0  | 0 / 0  |

That is 1 failure and 0 hangs. Its first failure:

```text
    a_test.go:16: boom
```

It reproduces with:

```sh
flaky stress -tags unit -run '^TestAToo$' -cpu 1 -load 1 -count 4 ./a
taskset -c 0 go -C . test -race -cover -count=4 -cpu 1 -timeout 2m0s -run '^TestAToo$' ./a
```

## Why

This hasn't been triaged.

## Expected

`TestAToo` passes on every run, at every CPU count and load.

